    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hi, I run a small online stationery shop based in Lyon and I'm a bit overwhelmed by GDPR. Can you give me a quick summary of the core principles I need to follow, specifically regarding how I handle customer email addresses and shipping info for orders? I have an audit coming up soon so I need to make sure I'm doing things right.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "GDPR, in short, is about respecting the personal data of your customers, which is crucial for your online shop. You must ensure you are collecting and using customer email addresses and shipping info only for the specific purposes you told them about, like fulfilling orders. It's vital to have a clear, concise privacy policy explaining exactly what data you hold and why, and you must get explicit consent before sending marketing emails. If you're using a third-party shipping provider, you need to make sure they are also GDPR compliant too.",
