    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that makes sense. One thing I'm worried about is data security—specifically the \"hidden\" risks. Like, if I'm not careful, could there be ways that data could be accessed or leaked without me even realizing it? How do I protect against those kinds of sneaky or invisible threats to my customer info?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hidden risks in data security often come from overlooked weak points, like a poorly secured password on your e-commerce platform or an unpatched plugin. To protect against these sneaky threats, you must prioritize robust security measures, which means using strong, unique passwords and enabling two-factor authentication everywhere possible. Furthermore, ensure your website hosting and any software you use are regularly updated—outdated software is a prime target for those invisible data thieves. Think of it like locking up your shop: you need strong locks on the main door, but you also need to check the tiny, forgotten back windows.",
      "source": "target",
